WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:13.885
Pinocchio could not sleep.

2
00:00:13.886 --> 00:00:19.137
He kept thinking of the money tree and the wonderful presents he would buy.

3
00:00:19.138 --> 00:00:23.752
"Oh, I can't wait to see my money tree," he said.

4
00:00:23.753 --> 00:00:26.881
But, he could not leave.

5
00:00:26.882 --> 00:00:33.200
"You must wait for sunlight before you go to the field," the cat had said.

6
00:00:33.201 --> 00:00:42.942
"Yes, if you see the field before sunlight, the magic tree will die," the fox had agreed.

7
00:00:42.943 --> 00:00:47.069
So Pinocchio waited and waited.

8
00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:52.384
As soon as the sun came up, Pinocchio ran all the way to the Field of Follies.

9
00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.664
He didn't stop once.

10
00:00:54.665 --> 00:01:01.566
"Here is the field," Pinocchio said, "but, where is my money tree?"

11
00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:05.728
He looked all over the field, but saw nothing that looked like a money tree.

12
00:01:05.729 --> 00:01:10.160
"I know this is the right field," he said, puzzled.

13
00:01:10.161 --> 00:01:12.990
"Maybe the gold forgot to grow!

14
00:01:12.991 --> 00:01:15.886
I will dig it out."

15
00:01:15.887 --> 00:01:18.946
So Pinocchio got down and began to dig.

16
00:01:18.947 --> 00:01:22.386
He dug and dug until he was covered in dirt.

17
00:01:22.387 --> 00:01:25.861
This hole was five times as big as the first hole.

18
00:01:25.862 --> 00:01:28.302
But he saw no gold!

19
00:01:28.303 --> 00:01:30.791
"I know this is the right place!

20
00:01:30.792 --> 00:01:36.339
Oh! Where is my gold?" Pinocchio cried.

21
00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.777
Above his head, someone was laughing.

22
00:01:38.778 --> 00:01:42.085
Pinocchio looked up and saw Mr. Cricket.

23
00:01:42.086 --> 00:01:45.483
"What are you doing here?" Pinocchio shouted.

24
00:01:45.484 --> 00:01:49.399
"And why are you laughing at me?"

25
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:54.187
"You are a foolish boy, Pinocchio," Mr. Cricket replied.

26
00:01:54.188 --> 00:01:58.749
"I tried to warn you about bad friends and bad choices.

27
00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.279
But you didn't listen to me.

28
00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.568
The fox and cat have stolen your gold.

29
00:02:04.569 --> 00:02:07.978
They are very far away by now."

30
00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:13.069
"Oh no! Oh no!" Pinocchio said.

31
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.745
He sat in the dirt and cried.

32
00:02:16.746 --> 00:02:19.015
"I must tell the police.

33
00:02:19.016 --> 00:02:21.846
They will help me."

34
00:02:21.847 --> 00:02:25.971
So Pinocchio ran off to the nearest town and went to the jail.

35
00:02:25.972 --> 00:02:28.279
He told the police his story.

36
00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.825
But, they did not help Pinocchio find his gold.

37
00:02:30.826 --> 00:02:33.606
They locked him in prison!

38
00:02:33.607 --> 00:02:37.296
"Ha-ha-ha. What a foolish boy.

39
00:02:37.297 --> 00:02:42.271
Looks like another tip for us, huh, partner?" one said to the other.

40
00:02:42.272 --> 00:02:44.582
"No, you don't understand.

41
00:02:44.583 --> 00:02:46.288
I did nothing wrong!

42
00:02:46.289 --> 00:02:51.419
Please! Help me find my gold," Pinocchio said.

43
00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:59.434
"Nope, you are stuck here for the rest of your life!" the jailer said, laughing.

44
00:02:59.435 --> 00:03:04.092
Pinocchio didn't know that the fox and cat owned this town.

45
00:03:04.093 --> 00:03:07.789
They paid the jailers for locking up people they had robbed.

46
00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:12.896
The police had become very rich because of the fox and cat.

47
00:03:12.897 --> 00:03:15.270
Pinocchio sat in prison all day.

48
00:03:15.271 --> 00:03:16.845
But he didn't cry.

49
00:03:16.846 --> 00:03:21.439
He looked out at the stars and said, "Mr. Cricket is right.

50
00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.789
I have been a foolish boy.

51
00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:26.543
I have made bad choices.

52
00:03:26.544 --> 00:03:30.684
It is my fault the gold is gone.

53
00:03:30.685 --> 00:03:33.341
If only someone would save me.

54
00:03:33.342 --> 00:03:36.766
I know I will be a good boy from now on.

55
00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:43.964
Please, is anyone listening? I need help."

56
00:03:43.965 --> 00:03:48.118
"Yes, I am listening," said a pretty voice.

57
00:03:48.119 --> 00:03:53.086
Just then, Pinocchio saw a small blue light fly by his window.

58
00:03:53.087 --> 00:03:56.079
"Who is out there?" he asked.

59
00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.299
"I am the Blue Fairy.

60
00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.592
I protect good children from harm.

61
00:04:01.593 --> 00:04:04.605
I am here to help you."

62
00:04:04.606 --> 00:04:09.707
"Please, get me out of jail," said Pinocchio.

63
00:04:09.708 --> 00:04:13.012
"Why are you in jail?" asked the fairy.

64
00:04:13.013 --> 00:04:15.529
"What have you done wrong?"

65
00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:18.964
"Nothing at all," said Pinocchio.

66
00:04:18.965 --> 00:04:21.853
"The fox and the cat tricked me.

67
00:04:21.854 --> 00:04:25.288
They stole all my gold coins."

68
00:04:25.289 --> 00:04:29.854
"Where did you get the money?" asked the Blue Fairy.

69
00:04:29.855 --> 00:04:34.940
"I earned it," said Pinocchio. "I starred in a show."

70
00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.933
Pinocchio's nose suddenly started to grow.

71
00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:41.101
Within seconds, it was six inches long!

72
00:04:41.102 --> 00:04:45.507
Pioncchio stared at his nose in surprise.

73
00:04:45.508 --> 00:04:52.672
Calmly, the Blue Fairy asked, "Did your father say you could work in the theater?"

74
00:04:52.673 --> 00:04:56.072
"Oh yes, Blue Fairy," said Pinocchio.

75
00:04:56.073 --> 00:05:00.180
"My father told me I would be a great actor!"

76
00:05:00.181 --> 00:05:03.843
His nose grew even longer at this new lie.

77
00:05:03.844 --> 00:05:08.147
Soon, Pinocchio's nose was eight inches long!

78
00:05:08.148 --> 00:05:15.096
"What's happening to my nose?" Pinocchio screamed.
